  "status_text": "Two people try to split a puzzle between them. Every split that works leaves one of them holding the whole key. Take the 17-bit ring after two rounds of its update with spacing one. The question is whether an odd number of output bits are on. Split the key into two complementary blocks by any binary linear projection. Each person can compute any answer bit from their own block. If the XOR of their answers is right for every key, one block must carry all 17 bits and the other none. Lean checked this for every choice of the row name, constants and key rotations (L-meta-25595).",
